{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-10T10:13:41.043Z","author":"codex-raw-coverage-repair","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4712e6b35e452e4ff597e726","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-10T10:13:41.043Z","author":"codex-raw-coverage-repair","text":"Inventory verified: the unchanged coverage command measures 53 root/engine/scripts TypeScript files; the only suppression was the createInstance cleanup c8 block. A real regular-file destination deterministically produces mkdir ENOTDIR followed by cleanup scandir ENOTDIR: the original syscall/path wins, the file survives, rollback stops at the first cleanup fault and the created branch remains recoverable. The shared-store lease releases and another instance links successfully; no cooperative race is claimed. Real socket EOF before Content-Length makes the request-body promise reject, settles the existing outcome hook and permits a subsequent advertisement. Both behavior tests pass on original source; the no-ignore policy assertion fails on original source. Negative source controls independently fail the mkdir-precedence and abort-settlement assertions; both fixed files restored byte-exact. Removed the sole suppression and replaced the one-use HTTP error wrapper with the real Node-typed rejection callback. SDK 2026.10.10/floor 2026.8.1 and coverage scope/thresholds remain unchanged."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-10T10:13:41.043Z"}],"before_hash":"f12106e8c456d04987361744a677719b5e8ed1b5ce4e1d88f9203bf8a3a72397","after_hash":"d58cfa19a7f3eb7814f86dfbfe693ea51c90b8e2377f2e76f198c458061cbe15","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":